# Threat to detect
A PowerShell script modifies Group Policy-related settings on a Windows host.
Adversaries abuse GPO modifications to disable security controls, escalate
privileges, or persist in the environment — for example, by tampering with
SmartScreen settings or with Group Policy refresh intervals to delay enforcement
of legitimate policies.

# Target environment
- Product: Windows
- Log source category: PowerShell Script Block Logging (ps_script)
- Requires Script Block Logging to be enabled — mention this requirement in the
  rule.
- Detection must rely on the textual content of the executed script block.
- The behavior is characterized by BOTH a registry path under the Group Policy
  system hive AND specific policy value names being touched. The rule should
  require both conditions together, not either one alone.

